1
00:00:05,666 --> 00:00:09,895
(Hwang In Youp)

2
00:00:09,896 --> 00:00:15,076
(Lee Hye Ri)

3
00:00:16,906 --> 00:00:21,976
(Baek Sung Chul, Lee Yul Eum)

4
00:00:35,096 --> 00:00:39,125
(Dream To You)

5
00:00:39,126 --> 00:00:40,126
(All people, events, and backgrounds are fictional.)

6
00:00:40,127 --> 00:00:41,135
(This drama includes footage created using AI.)

7
00:00:41,136 --> 00:00:42,136
(Children and animals were filmed under strict safety guidelines.)

8
00:00:43,806 --> 00:00:45,236
Don't go, Yi Jae.

9
00:00:45,866 --> 00:00:46,906
Okay?

10
00:00:56,616 --> 00:00:57,616
Su Bin.

11
00:01:00,616 --> 00:01:02,156
I love you,

12
00:01:04,226 --> 00:01:05,686
but my dream isn't you.

13
00:01:11,196 --> 00:01:13,326
(Final Episode)

14
00:01:16,696 --> 00:01:23,706
(Gyeongseong Love Song Special Screening)

15
00:01:28,376 --> 00:01:29,446
Even if you leave,

16
00:01:30,046 --> 00:01:31,316
I'm not giving up on us.

17
00:01:32,686 --> 00:01:33,686
You know what that means, right?

18
00:01:34,056 --> 00:01:35,356
I guess you don't.

19
00:01:36,386 --> 00:01:37,656
Me leaving...

20
00:01:38,426 --> 00:01:39,786
means I'm letting us go.

21
00:01:40,156 --> 00:01:41,556
It's only two years.

22
00:01:43,056 --> 00:01:46,196
- Why do we have to break up? - If I keep holding your hand,

23
00:01:46,496 --> 00:01:49,496
I'll want to lean on you. Then nothing will change.

24
00:01:49,736 --> 00:01:50,736
See?

25
00:01:50,806 --> 00:01:53,306
You just took that chair right from me.

26
00:01:53,736 --> 00:01:56,536
- So what? - Su Bin, do you really not get it?

27
00:01:57,176 --> 00:01:59,476
If I'm with you, you only focus on me.

28
00:01:59,806 --> 00:02:00,976
Are you going to live like this forever?

29
00:02:01,076 --> 00:02:02,046
Only ever looking at me?

30
00:02:05,186 --> 00:02:07,216
This isn't how I pictured us.

31
00:02:08,616 --> 00:02:09,656
This is for my sake,

32
00:02:10,526 --> 00:02:11,526
but you can't keep living like this either.

33
00:02:11,586 --> 00:02:13,826
Why do you keep saying I can't go on like this?

34
00:02:17,666 --> 00:02:18,666
You said you like me.

35
00:02:22,536 --> 00:02:25,706
- You said you love me. - So I'm going to stop loving you!

36
00:02:34,346 --> 00:02:36,276
Why are you making me say something like this?

37
00:02:39,286 --> 00:02:41,216
I'm sorry. I'm leaving.

38
00:02:43,926 --> 00:02:47,826
(Gyeongseong Love Song Special Screening)

39
00:03:04,006 --> 00:03:05,906
(2026 Bunam City International Cinema Residency)

40
00:03:06,006 --> 00:03:07,246
(Destination: Montreal)

41
00:03:07,846 --> 00:03:09,016
(I apply for the Bunam City International Cinema Residency.)

42
00:03:14,986 --> 00:03:17,586
(Applicant Name: Joo Yi Jae)

43
00:03:30,736 --> 00:03:32,835
You're not leaving me out on purpose...

44
00:03:32,836 --> 00:03:34,236
because you're worried my leg might hurt, are you?

45
00:03:34,476 --> 00:03:37,576
Gosh, I just said she graduated from a no-name university.

46
00:03:37,776 --> 00:03:39,746
It's not like I said anything wrong!

47
00:03:40,946 --> 00:03:44,746
No, no one says a thing. Isn't that strange?

48
00:03:45,246 --> 00:03:47,416
Who I am, how or why I became the director here.

49
00:03:47,486 --> 00:03:48,816
Nobody asks!

50
00:03:48,956 --> 00:03:50,056
So help me, Woo Su Bin.

51
00:03:52,026 --> 00:03:53,486
So I can start running again.

52
00:04:09,676 --> 00:04:15,946
(Gyeongseong Love Song Special Screening)

53
00:04:16,046 --> 00:04:17,046
Yes, Music Director.

54
00:04:17,486 --> 00:04:19,916
It's about the guitar piece for the reunion scene.

55
00:04:20,716 --> 00:04:22,956
I tried my best to remove the noise,

56
00:04:23,116 --> 00:04:25,386
but I couldn't get rid of all the background sound.

57
00:04:25,456 --> 00:04:27,626
Well, that's my job.

58
00:04:27,756 --> 00:04:30,156
You can just send me the video file, Director.

59
00:04:30,296 --> 00:04:31,666
Then I'll send it to you right now.

60
00:04:32,226 --> 00:04:34,236
And I had an idea while working on it.

61
00:04:34,596 --> 00:04:37,466
Since we can't get a clean recording anyway,

62
00:04:37,906 --> 00:04:40,636
- let's make it like a gramophone. - A gramophone?

63
00:04:40,936 --> 00:04:41,936
Yes.

64
00:04:42,006 --> 00:04:46,046
That way, the audio quality issue would be naturally masked,

65
00:04:46,106 --> 00:04:47,576
and it would also enhance the period feel.

66
00:04:47,676 --> 00:04:50,686
Then please discuss it with Director Woo and let me know.

67
00:04:50,746 --> 00:04:52,146
Yes, Director. Oh, right.

68
00:04:52,446 --> 00:04:53,516
By the way,

69
00:04:53,716 --> 00:04:54,886
is something wrong with Director Woo?

70
00:04:55,656 --> 00:04:57,626
I'm not sure.

71
00:04:58,256 --> 00:05:00,386
- Why? - It's just that he seems...

72
00:05:02,296 --> 00:05:04,726
It's nothing. Anyway, I'll be in touch.

73
00:05:04,896 --> 00:05:05,966
Thank you, Director.

74
00:05:06,266 --> 00:05:07,266
Okay.

75
00:05:12,966 --> 00:05:18,446
(Gyeongseong Love Song Special Screening)

76
00:05:30,726 --> 00:05:33,726
Okay. All right!

77
00:05:34,156 --> 00:05:35,526
Let's see.

78
00:05:35,756 --> 00:05:36,795
Hold on.

79
00:05:36,796 --> 00:05:37,796
Oh, seriously!

80
00:05:37,866 --> 00:05:40,426
Gosh, you scared me! Director!

81
00:05:40,496 --> 00:05:42,136
Gosh, you scared me.

82
00:05:43,296 --> 00:05:45,336
Hey, so I was thinking about something.

83
00:05:45,406 --> 00:05:48,106
What, are you talking in your sleep?

84
00:05:48,276 --> 00:05:50,206
Seriously, why are you sleeping here again?

85
00:05:50,276 --> 00:05:51,706
Just go home already!

86
00:05:51,906 --> 00:05:55,176
Listen. You know that guitar scene we decided to use?

87
00:05:55,616 --> 00:05:58,116
If we can't get a clean version of it anyway,

88
00:05:58,216 --> 00:06:01,316
why don't we just make it sound like it's from a gramophone?

89
00:06:02,256 --> 00:06:03,856
Like it's coming from the street.

90
00:06:05,986 --> 00:06:08,296
Did you already talk to Director Joo?

91
00:06:09,156 --> 00:06:10,256
What?

92
00:06:10,396 --> 00:06:11,625
No, it's just that you're saying...

93
00:06:11,626 --> 00:06:13,166
the exact same thing as Director Joo.

94
00:06:13,866 --> 00:06:16,536
Actually, I just came to work on that, among other things.

95
00:06:18,306 --> 00:06:20,036
- I see. - By the way,

96
00:06:21,136 --> 00:06:24,346
who on earth is Sim Shin?

97
00:06:24,746 --> 00:06:27,576
Where did you find this hidden gem?

98
00:06:28,416 --> 00:06:30,016
Why are you so close?

99
00:06:31,246 --> 00:06:32,246
He's...

100
00:06:32,916 --> 00:06:34,616
Sim Yu Geon's father.

101
00:06:36,156 --> 00:06:38,126
No way. Really?

102
00:06:38,186 --> 00:06:40,386
No wonder his playing was so extraordinary.

103
00:06:40,796 --> 00:06:42,756
I mean, his technique isn't flashy,

104
00:06:42,856 --> 00:06:45,296
but you know how it just digs deep into your soul?

105
00:06:45,526 --> 00:06:47,866
Hold on. I'm so excited!

106
00:06:48,466 --> 00:06:49,496
Inspiration has finally struck.

107
00:06:53,106 --> 00:06:54,106
Right!

108
00:06:54,676 --> 00:06:57,806
- I need to work. Could you leave? - Yes, go ahead.

109
00:06:57,876 --> 00:06:59,506
Let's make some magic.

110
00:07:00,446 --> 00:07:01,545
If you're going to be here,

111
00:07:01,546 --> 00:07:02,976
you could at least help with the rent.

112
00:07:03,046 --> 00:07:06,145
You always miss your deadlines if I'm not nagging you.

113
00:07:06,146 --> 00:07:08,186
- Hurry and turn on your computer. - Okay, here.

114
00:07:08,416 --> 00:07:11,956
When Mu Gyeom is being chased by the officer.

115
00:07:15,396 --> 00:07:17,126
- Hey! - Is this supposed to be Africa?

116
00:07:18,026 --> 00:07:19,826
This is the Gyeongseong era.

117
00:07:19,996 --> 00:07:23,196
Gosh, you really know nothing about music.

118
00:07:27,876 --> 00:07:29,276
(2026 Bunam City International Cinema Residency)

119
00:07:29,336 --> 00:07:31,145
(Final Evaluation Results)

120
00:07:31,146 --> 00:07:33,406
(Congratulations on your acceptance, Director Joo Yi Jae.)

121
00:07:45,726 --> 00:07:47,496
(A director's certificate...)

122
00:07:50,896 --> 00:07:54,166
("Dream", written by Woo Su Bin)

123
00:08:00,066 --> 00:08:01,076
Woo Su Bin.

124
00:08:20,896 --> 00:08:24,566
("Dream")

125
00:08:32,406 --> 00:08:33,406
Can I come in?

126
00:08:35,006 --> 00:08:36,176
Yes, come in.

127
00:08:40,376 --> 00:08:42,176
Sorry. That wasn't my place to say.

128
00:08:43,576 --> 00:08:44,946
Looks like you got in.

129
00:08:46,386 --> 00:08:47,656
Is that what you came to tell me?

130
00:08:48,616 --> 00:08:49,616
Yes.

131
00:08:52,526 --> 00:08:53,526
Yi Jae.

132
00:08:55,156 --> 00:08:56,296
Why the long face?

133
00:08:58,466 --> 00:08:59,466
I'm sorry.

134
00:09:05,836 --> 00:09:06,836
Look at me.

135
00:09:09,836 --> 00:09:11,076
I was wrong.

136
00:09:13,976 --> 00:09:15,575
My feelings for you were the only thing...

137
00:09:15,576 --> 00:09:16,646
that brought me here,

138
00:09:18,246 --> 00:09:20,986
but now, for that same reason, I just told you to stay here.

139
00:09:21,756 --> 00:09:22,916
I felt so ashamed of myself.

140
00:09:24,686 --> 00:09:26,686
That promise I made to give you back your dream.

141
00:09:27,426 --> 00:09:28,526
I forgot about it for a moment.

142
00:09:30,256 --> 00:09:31,266
I'm sorry.

143
00:09:32,296 --> 00:09:34,696
No. You've already given it back to me.

144
00:09:35,966 --> 00:09:37,606
This dream I rediscovered thanks to you.

145
00:09:38,736 --> 00:09:39,736
I'm going to make it...

146
00:09:40,466 --> 00:09:42,436
even bigger and better for the next two years.

147
00:09:50,276 --> 00:09:51,886
I have no doubt that you will.

148
00:09:53,716 --> 00:09:55,516
I can tell just by how you're shining right now.

149
00:10:09,536 --> 00:10:11,236
Goodbye, Director Joo Yi Jae.

150
00:10:12,606 --> 00:10:15,676
Wherever you are, whatever you do, I'll be rooting for you.

151
00:10:17,946 --> 00:10:18,946
Thank you.

152
00:10:22,116 --> 00:10:23,116
Take care.

153
00:10:42,996 --> 00:10:49,306
("Dream", written by Woo Su Bin)

154
00:11:03,686 --> 00:11:05,486
(Gyeongseong Love Song)

155
00:11:05,556 --> 00:11:08,656
I finally finished it!

156
00:11:14,536 --> 00:11:15,536
Cut.

157
00:11:15,596 --> 00:11:16,666
- Okay. - Okay.

158
00:11:34,816 --> 00:11:38,056
(Director Woo Su Bin, Director Joo Yi Jae)

159
00:11:39,856 --> 00:11:40,856
Joo Yi Jae.

160
00:11:55,636 --> 00:11:56,636
Here.

161
00:11:57,876 --> 00:11:58,876
Take it.

162
00:12:00,646 --> 00:12:02,376
Rather than holding you back,

163
00:12:03,516 --> 00:12:04,716
I hope this gives you...

164
00:12:06,786 --> 00:12:08,056
the strength to keep going.

165
00:12:09,586 --> 00:12:11,556
Just like Gyeongseong Love Song did for me.

166
00:12:57,936 --> 00:12:59,436
Did you tell your dad...

167
00:12:59,966 --> 00:13:02,306
that his performance will be in our movie?

168
00:13:02,576 --> 00:13:05,146
Yes. My dad was so happy.

169
00:13:06,646 --> 00:13:08,076
He watches the video...

170
00:13:08,616 --> 00:13:09,946
you filmed for him every day in his hospital room.

171
00:13:10,246 --> 00:13:11,516
I'm glad he likes it.

172
00:13:13,616 --> 00:13:18,786
(Simsim Seafood)

173
00:13:19,126 --> 00:13:20,126
Yi Jae.

174
00:13:20,726 --> 00:13:22,056
You know I'm your number one fan, right?

175
00:13:23,556 --> 00:13:24,566
I know.

176
00:13:25,126 --> 00:13:27,666
When I had no one else in Seoul,

177
00:13:28,566 --> 00:13:30,466
I wouldn't have made it if it weren't for you.

178
00:13:31,936 --> 00:13:33,666
Pretending you couldn't finish it all,

179
00:13:33,836 --> 00:13:35,106
you would bring me fried chicken.

180
00:13:36,376 --> 00:13:39,406
Even when you had nothing to say, you would call me all the time.

181
00:13:40,476 --> 00:13:41,976
I know it was all your way of supporting me.

182
00:13:47,016 --> 00:13:48,016
So,

183
00:13:49,186 --> 00:13:50,586
if you get lonely or things get tough over there,

184
00:13:51,226 --> 00:13:52,456
you have to tell me.

185
00:13:53,686 --> 00:13:55,756
Hey, this is Joo Yi Jae you're talking to.

186
00:13:55,826 --> 00:13:57,696
I know. That's exactly why I'm telling you.

187
00:13:58,066 --> 00:13:59,626
You hate showing any weakness,

188
00:14:00,366 --> 00:14:01,996
so don't just grit your teeth and bear it alone.

189
00:14:04,806 --> 00:14:06,206
What is all this? So cheesy.

190
00:14:07,506 --> 00:14:08,606
Just eat your stew.

191
00:14:18,516 --> 00:14:19,816
Hey, Joo Yeong Jae!

192
00:14:19,886 --> 00:14:20,886
What?

193
00:14:20,946 --> 00:14:23,656
You running a restaurant? You should just quit.

194
00:14:23,716 --> 00:14:26,486
- Gosh! - What's with you? What's wrong?

195
00:14:27,486 --> 00:14:28,496
Did you even taste this?

196
00:14:28,626 --> 00:14:30,696
Did you taste it before serving it? Here!

197
00:14:31,066 --> 00:14:33,496
Well, if it isn't the great food critic.

198
00:14:39,806 --> 00:14:41,976
Gosh! Water!

199
00:14:42,506 --> 00:14:44,136
Hey, water!

200
00:14:48,576 --> 00:14:49,616
I'll go add some water.

201
00:14:50,376 --> 00:14:51,646
Sorry about that.

202
00:14:54,486 --> 00:14:55,486
Sorry.

203
00:14:57,386 --> 00:14:59,326
You said you're staying for two years,

204
00:14:59,386 --> 00:15:00,586
so why are you only packing winter clothes?

205
00:15:01,256 --> 00:15:02,426
I looked it up,

206
00:15:02,496 --> 00:15:04,966
and it said Montreal has four distinct seasons too.

207
00:15:05,526 --> 00:15:07,066
It's pronounced Montreal, you idiot.

208
00:15:07,796 --> 00:15:08,796
Let her be.

209
00:15:08,866 --> 00:15:09,996
She can just buy them when she gets there.

210
00:15:10,436 --> 00:15:12,836
Since when does our mom tell you to buy things?

211
00:15:13,266 --> 00:15:16,206
Mom, I can't take it all with me anyway.

212
00:15:16,276 --> 00:15:18,746
Why can't you take it? It's not like you're carrying it.

213
00:15:18,806 --> 00:15:19,906
The airplane is.

214
00:15:20,006 --> 00:15:21,716
They have Korean food everywhere these days.

215
00:15:21,776 --> 00:15:23,046
They have everything there.

216
00:15:29,116 --> 00:15:32,286
- In that case, take this. - What is it?

217
00:15:32,426 --> 00:15:33,825
- Hey. - Is this money?

218
00:15:33,826 --> 00:15:35,456
Give it here. It's for your sister.

219
00:15:35,726 --> 00:15:38,266
This has to be a thousand dollars!

220
00:15:41,026 --> 00:15:43,866
Unbelievable. Mom, you don't have money to spare.

221
00:15:44,096 --> 00:15:45,466
Use this to pay off your loan interest.

222
00:15:46,436 --> 00:15:48,076
Just keep it for emergencies.

223
00:15:48,136 --> 00:15:50,076
Don't go pinching pennies in a foreign country.

224
00:15:50,506 --> 00:15:52,346
I said I'm fine.

225
00:15:52,406 --> 00:15:53,845
It's not like I'm leaving for good. I'll be back soon,

226
00:15:53,846 --> 00:15:55,645
so why are you making such a big deal?

227
00:15:55,646 --> 00:15:58,216
She's right. Two years will fly by.

228
00:15:58,446 --> 00:16:00,646
Just think of it as her doing military service.

229
00:16:00,786 --> 00:16:01,786
Mom, when I was discharged,

230
00:16:01,856 --> 00:16:04,156
- you said, "You're back already?" - It's not the same.

231
00:16:05,026 --> 00:16:06,956
You only give me a hard time.

232
00:16:07,556 --> 00:16:08,826
Oh, honestly. You.

233
00:16:09,556 --> 00:16:11,726
When your mother gives you something, just take it.

234
00:16:12,666 --> 00:16:13,866
I haven't done anything for you all your life,

235
00:16:13,926 --> 00:16:15,366
and it breaks my heart.

236
00:16:16,236 --> 00:16:17,236
All right.

237
00:16:17,966 --> 00:16:19,336
I'll take everything.

238
00:16:23,576 --> 00:16:24,676
What do you want to eat?

239
00:16:25,246 --> 00:16:26,546
Let's just eat.

240
00:16:27,446 --> 00:16:28,616
Kimchi fried rice.

241
00:16:28,946 --> 00:16:30,046
Oh, dear.

242
00:16:31,416 --> 00:16:34,186
Joo Yeong Jae. Come here and chop some kimchi.

243
00:16:34,286 --> 00:16:36,586
Mom, I've been chopping things all day.

244
00:16:36,986 --> 00:16:38,026
Hurry up and go.

245
00:16:44,466 --> 00:16:45,726
Chop it finely.

246
00:16:46,196 --> 00:16:47,266
Yes, ma'am.

247
00:17:00,646 --> 00:17:03,046
To hold a certain man in my arms,

248
00:17:03,876 --> 00:17:06,886
I never dreamed I had to risk my life, take up a gun,

249
00:17:07,016 --> 00:17:10,286
and cross the border.

250
00:17:12,856 --> 00:17:14,856
You are truly a remarkable man.

251
00:17:17,756 --> 00:17:22,436
So fearless. You are a truly remarkable woman.

252
00:17:23,066 --> 00:17:24,296
What are you doing?

253
00:17:25,306 --> 00:17:26,836
Hurry and hold me.

254
00:18:05,606 --> 00:18:08,876
(Written and directed by Woo Su Bin, Joo Yi Jae)

255
00:18:31,036 --> 00:18:32,866
- Great work. - Thanks.

256
00:18:33,166 --> 00:18:35,776
- The movie is great. - Thank you.

257
00:18:36,206 --> 00:18:39,546
We should have no problem releasing it this year.

258
00:18:41,716 --> 00:18:45,046
- Director Woo, great job. - You worked hard.

259
00:18:46,046 --> 00:18:47,046
- Thanks. - Well then,

260
00:18:47,047 --> 00:18:48,986
let's move somewhere else to talk in more detail.

261
00:18:49,056 --> 00:18:51,056
Yes, let's continue our conversation over a meal.

262
00:18:51,326 --> 00:18:52,926
I've made a reservation,

263
00:18:52,986 --> 00:18:54,356
so let's all head over there together.

264
00:18:54,696 --> 00:18:55,826
Let's go.

265
00:19:16,416 --> 00:19:17,446
Ian.

266
00:19:20,046 --> 00:19:21,856
I shouldn't be saying this as the CEO,

267
00:19:23,016 --> 00:19:24,656
but in life, if you have a chance to go,

268
00:19:24,756 --> 00:19:25,926
you should just go.

269
00:19:27,126 --> 00:19:29,626
It's not too late. Go to Yi Jae.

270
00:19:31,766 --> 00:19:33,126
Just go!

271
00:19:36,366 --> 00:19:37,366
Okay.

272
00:19:38,606 --> 00:19:39,636
Hey, Ian.

273
00:19:40,306 --> 00:19:43,406
How are you going to get there? Are you going to run to the airport?

274
00:19:43,676 --> 00:19:45,606
You really wouldn't survive without me. Here.

275
00:19:57,386 --> 00:19:59,056
(Applicant Recommendation)

276
00:19:59,156 --> 00:20:01,926
I love the world that Director Joo Yi Jae creates.

277
00:20:03,596 --> 00:20:07,126
She finds warmth even in a world full of zombies,

278
00:20:08,136 --> 00:20:10,196
and even in an era full of despair,

279
00:20:10,666 --> 00:20:13,866
she is someone who ultimately discovers hope.

280
00:20:27,746 --> 00:20:29,356
She clearly has...

281
00:20:29,616 --> 00:20:31,786
a special perspective that is all her own.

282
00:20:33,056 --> 00:20:36,556
To be able to be a part of Director Joo Yi Jae's world...

283
00:20:37,256 --> 00:20:39,496
was a great honour for me as well.

284
00:20:40,796 --> 00:20:43,396
(Incheon International Airport)

285
00:20:45,866 --> 00:20:49,436
I still wish I could remain in her world,

286
00:20:51,806 --> 00:20:53,946
and I still find it hard to let her go,

287
00:20:58,616 --> 00:21:00,146
- but I know she's destined... - Thank you.

288
00:21:00,216 --> 00:21:02,556
for greater things in a bigger world,

289
00:21:03,256 --> 00:21:06,856
so I want to cheer for Director Joo Yi Jae's future.

290
00:22:47,456 --> 00:22:49,396
I can say without a doubt,

291
00:22:51,326 --> 00:22:52,496
Director Joo was...

292
00:22:52,796 --> 00:22:54,596
the best partner I've ever had in my entire life.

293
00:22:54,626 --> 00:22:58,836
(Director Joo was the best partner I've ever had in my entire life.)

294
00:23:24,696 --> 00:23:26,126
(You can do it, Joo Yi Jae.)

295
00:23:26,196 --> 00:23:27,666
(Seeing it through to the end is what makes it great.)

296
00:23:27,726 --> 00:23:28,736
(Dream)

297
00:24:44,306 --> 00:24:47,206
(Final Draft Completed, Thursday, December 3, 2026)

298
00:24:53,186 --> 00:24:55,886
(Friday, Gyeongseong Love Song Premiere, 8pm)

299
00:25:03,996 --> 00:25:05,466
(Gyeongseong Love Song)

300
00:25:05,526 --> 00:25:06,996
(VIP Premiere)

301
00:25:07,066 --> 00:25:08,436
Thank you all so much for coming...

302
00:25:08,496 --> 00:25:10,466
to the VIP premiere of Gyeongseong Love Song.

303
00:25:10,536 --> 00:25:11,636
Now then,

304
00:25:11,806 --> 00:25:14,206
let's welcome our director and the cast.

305
00:25:14,266 --> 00:25:16,436
Please give them a big round of applause.

306
00:25:17,576 --> 00:25:20,606
You're so handsome, Woo Su Bin!

307
00:25:20,906 --> 00:25:22,676
Gyeongseong Love Song.

308
00:25:24,046 --> 00:25:25,886
Ten million tickets.

309
00:25:26,446 --> 00:25:29,986
- Ten million! Let's go. - Hello.

310
00:25:30,056 --> 00:25:31,415
I'm Woo Su Bin,

311
00:25:31,416 --> 00:25:32,686
the director of the film Gyeongseong Love Song.

312
00:25:33,326 --> 00:25:35,196
Our co-director, Joo Yi Jae,

313
00:25:35,256 --> 00:25:37,956
was unfortunately unable to join us today.

314
00:25:38,226 --> 00:25:40,226
We ask for your understanding.

315
00:25:40,596 --> 00:25:42,296
Since you've taken your precious time to be here,

316
00:25:42,366 --> 00:25:44,966
I hope you laugh and cry to your heart's content.

317
00:25:45,306 --> 00:25:48,336
Now then, from action to romance,

318
00:25:48,406 --> 00:25:50,706
our very own Actress Oh Ha Na can do it all.

319
00:25:50,776 --> 00:25:52,306
I'll pass the microphone to her.

320
00:25:53,076 --> 00:25:55,046
You're so pretty, Oh Ha Na!

321
00:25:56,276 --> 00:25:57,276
Yes, hello.

322
00:25:57,346 --> 00:25:59,016
Making my big-screen debut with this movie,

323
00:25:59,046 --> 00:26:01,285
I'm aiming for the title of Queen of Romance.

324
00:26:01,286 --> 00:26:02,556
I'm Oh Ha Na.

325
00:26:04,656 --> 00:26:05,756
Yes, hello.

326
00:26:05,826 --> 00:26:09,226
I play Mu Gyeom in Gyeongseong Love Song.

327
00:26:09,496 --> 00:26:11,296
I'm a rookie actor Sim Yu Geon.

328
00:26:11,356 --> 00:26:13,196
I hope you enjoy my performance. Thank you.

329
00:26:16,336 --> 00:26:18,096
All right, let's say our final goodbyes to the audience,

330
00:26:18,166 --> 00:26:20,006
and then we'll exit.

331
00:26:20,066 --> 00:26:21,436
Okay. One, two, three.

332
00:26:26,706 --> 00:26:30,476
Gosh, seriously. I wonder who their mother is.

333
00:26:30,876 --> 00:26:32,886
I must be lucky with my kids.

334
00:26:33,546 --> 00:26:34,716
Which one of the two?

335
00:26:35,716 --> 00:26:37,756
- Oh, you startled me. - Both of them, of course.

336
00:26:38,756 --> 00:26:42,056
- Who invited you? Seriously. - It's a happy occasion, CEO Ahn.

337
00:26:42,156 --> 00:26:44,926
- Seriously. Go away. - Chae Yeon, move aside a bit.

338
00:26:45,066 --> 00:26:46,166
CEO Ahn,

339
00:26:46,226 --> 00:26:48,296
your son and daughter take after you,

340
00:26:48,366 --> 00:26:51,496
- so they're handsome and pretty. - Hey, you.

341
00:26:52,036 --> 00:26:53,736
Oh, my, CEO Ahn. Did you switch salons?

342
00:26:53,866 --> 00:26:57,376
- Gosh, honestly. - I'll let it slide today, you punk.

343
00:26:57,436 --> 00:27:00,376
If Director Joo were here today,

344
00:27:00,646 --> 00:27:02,676
she would have greeted everyone at the top of her lungs.

345
00:27:03,716 --> 00:27:04,746
It's a bummer.

346
00:27:04,846 --> 00:27:05,986
I know, right?

347
00:27:06,046 --> 00:27:08,486
Director Joo sure had a powerful voice.

348
00:27:09,186 --> 00:27:10,356
Gosh.

349
00:27:10,416 --> 00:27:13,326
It feels like just yesterday when she dragged us all...

350
00:27:13,786 --> 00:27:15,056
to storm CEO Ahn's office.

351
00:27:15,796 --> 00:27:17,396
That was already a year ago.

352
00:27:19,126 --> 00:27:20,366
I wonder how she's doing.

353
00:27:23,836 --> 00:27:24,896
It's starting.

354
00:27:30,076 --> 00:27:31,206
Yi Jae.

355
00:27:31,676 --> 00:27:33,376
The premiere went well.

356
00:27:34,806 --> 00:27:36,746
The after-party was a madhouse.

357
00:27:38,346 --> 00:27:39,716
The Assistant Director...

358
00:27:40,146 --> 00:27:41,546
drank hard again today.

359
00:27:45,356 --> 00:27:48,726
Director, there's something I still regret.

360
00:27:49,956 --> 00:27:52,226
Back then, to Director Joo,

361
00:27:52,296 --> 00:27:54,666
I shouldn't have acted that way.

362
00:27:55,026 --> 00:27:59,006
You've already told me that more than ten times.

363
00:28:00,166 --> 00:28:02,406
I see.

364
00:28:05,076 --> 00:28:09,276
Anyway, she may be younger than me,

365
00:28:09,376 --> 00:28:12,886
but I think she's a really great person.

366
00:28:12,986 --> 00:28:15,356
After she already made her directorial debut,

367
00:28:15,416 --> 00:28:18,856
why would she go abroad to study more?

368
00:28:18,926 --> 00:28:21,386
That takes some serious guts, you know?

369
00:28:21,686 --> 00:28:24,396
I could never do it. Never.

370
00:28:25,796 --> 00:28:27,026
You've said that before too.

371
00:28:27,096 --> 00:28:28,866
Right.

372
00:28:28,936 --> 00:28:30,396
So I have.

373
00:28:30,796 --> 00:28:34,666
In that case, shall we continue this unfinished conversation...

374
00:28:34,736 --> 00:28:36,236
over a third round?

375
00:28:36,306 --> 00:28:37,906
The first round was official,

376
00:28:37,976 --> 00:28:39,506
and the second was out of courtesy,

377
00:28:39,846 --> 00:28:42,246
so I've done my duty for the night.

378
00:28:42,346 --> 00:28:44,876
Come on.

379
00:28:44,946 --> 00:28:47,386
The third round is for the memories,

380
00:28:47,446 --> 00:28:50,886
- and the fourth is for loyalty. - No, it's not.

381
00:28:52,526 --> 00:28:53,526
Let's call it a night.

382
00:28:53,586 --> 00:28:57,996
Gosh, I miss the loyal Director Joo.

383
00:28:58,866 --> 00:29:01,996
I wonder what time it is in Canada right now?

384
00:29:03,066 --> 00:29:04,736
Ten o'clock...

385
00:29:04,796 --> 00:29:08,836
Director Joo. Hey, Director Joo...

386
00:29:11,776 --> 00:29:14,006
(Director Joo)

387
00:29:24,786 --> 00:29:25,856
Hello?

388
00:29:28,456 --> 00:29:29,726
Hello?

389
00:29:30,296 --> 00:29:31,456
Assistant Director?

390
00:29:35,396 --> 00:29:37,336
Did you call me about the premiere today?

391
00:29:38,166 --> 00:29:39,366
How was it?

392
00:29:43,006 --> 00:29:44,006
What?

393
00:29:48,816 --> 00:29:50,476
Assistant Director.

394
00:29:52,946 --> 00:29:54,546
What? Was this a butt dial?

395
00:29:56,486 --> 00:29:58,656
This call is costing me a lot. I'm hanging up.

396
00:29:58,826 --> 00:30:01,426
(Director Joo)

397
00:30:04,696 --> 00:30:05,896
Would you know?

398
00:30:07,166 --> 00:30:08,426
(Director Joo)

399
00:30:08,496 --> 00:30:10,636
That for 24 seconds,

400
00:30:12,166 --> 00:30:13,736
we were together?

401
00:30:46,836 --> 00:30:47,836
What are you listening to?

402
00:30:51,276 --> 00:30:53,406
My dad's guitar performance.

403
00:30:54,046 --> 00:30:55,046
Really?

404
00:31:08,996 --> 00:31:11,796
(Gyeongseong Love Song)

405
00:31:19,736 --> 00:31:21,036
You can lean on me.

406
00:31:38,556 --> 00:31:39,786
Yu Geon.

407
00:31:41,356 --> 00:31:43,726
When should we eat our canned pineapple?

408
00:31:45,026 --> 00:31:47,096
In 10,000 years?

409
00:31:52,706 --> 00:31:54,206
Our main character...

410
00:31:54,936 --> 00:31:56,736
gets a full-on happy ending.

411
00:31:59,146 --> 00:32:00,545
("Gyeongseong Love Song Lovers Oh Ha Na and Sim Geon...")

412
00:32:00,546 --> 00:32:01,946
("Become a Real Couple")

413
00:32:03,176 --> 00:32:05,846
It'll probably be a happy ending.

414
00:32:06,416 --> 00:32:07,416
What?

415
00:32:08,386 --> 00:32:10,616
Sim Yu Geon!

416
00:32:12,656 --> 00:32:15,326
(CEO Ahn Soo Hee)

417
00:32:21,096 --> 00:32:23,696
(Book Search)

418
00:32:25,536 --> 00:32:27,106
(Choi Sa Rang)

419
00:32:28,236 --> 00:32:29,236
"Choi Sa Rang"?

420
00:32:31,736 --> 00:32:34,046
("Easy Love, Difficult Love")

421
00:32:40,116 --> 00:32:41,516
(Book Search)

422
00:32:42,886 --> 00:32:44,016
There we go.

423
00:32:46,756 --> 00:32:50,356
(Search: Choi Sa Rang)

424
00:32:51,126 --> 00:32:53,896
Yes! Now that's what I call marketing.

425
00:32:53,966 --> 00:32:55,996
I think I'm a genius.

426
00:32:56,566 --> 00:32:59,066
(Most Talked-About New Book in 2026)

427
00:32:59,106 --> 00:33:01,866
(New Fiction and Non-fiction)

428
00:33:03,536 --> 00:33:05,006
Where did they all go?

429
00:33:05,306 --> 00:33:06,506
Wait.

430
00:33:07,346 --> 00:33:08,376
Hey.

431
00:33:08,776 --> 00:33:10,446
Excuse me. I'm so sorry.

432
00:33:10,546 --> 00:33:12,546
It's just that my books have all vanished.

433
00:33:12,616 --> 00:33:14,586
The one called "Easy Love, Difficult Love."

434
00:33:14,746 --> 00:33:17,856
If you mean that book, that gentleman over there...

435
00:33:19,326 --> 00:33:21,756
("Easy Love, Difficult Love")

436
00:33:25,026 --> 00:33:26,426
In Wook?

437
00:33:31,936 --> 00:33:34,766
Well, you caught me.

438
00:33:45,946 --> 00:33:47,386
The two we knew...

439
00:33:47,916 --> 00:33:50,716
seem to have an open ending.

440
00:33:51,756 --> 00:33:53,326
(Gyeongseong Love Song)

441
00:33:53,386 --> 00:33:55,026
My next question...

442
00:33:55,056 --> 00:33:57,356
is something I'm personally curious about.

443
00:33:57,426 --> 00:33:59,766
In this project, you're not credited as Ian Woo,

444
00:33:59,826 --> 00:34:02,966
but as Woo Su Bin.

445
00:34:03,096 --> 00:34:07,366
- Is there a reason for that? - Now that I'm back in Korea,

446
00:34:07,536 --> 00:34:09,906
I wanted to be called by my name, Woo Su Bin.

447
00:34:11,136 --> 00:34:13,076
Every step I've taken...

448
00:34:13,146 --> 00:34:15,346
has been a step toward reclaiming my name, Woo Su Bin.

449
00:34:17,276 --> 00:34:18,476
Finally,

450
00:34:20,486 --> 00:34:21,516
I'm here.

451
00:34:28,356 --> 00:34:29,356
Yi Jae.

452
00:34:30,156 --> 00:34:31,526
I hope this...

453
00:34:32,126 --> 00:34:33,796
isn't my ending.

454
00:35:22,576 --> 00:35:25,416
I miss you, Yi Jae.

455
00:35:35,286 --> 00:35:36,456
I guess I still...

456
00:35:39,596 --> 00:35:41,326
haven't gotten over you.

457
00:35:45,496 --> 00:35:46,806
I guess I don't want to wake up...

458
00:35:48,306 --> 00:35:49,636
from my dreams.

459
00:36:10,696 --> 00:36:12,325
(1 year later)

460
00:36:12,326 --> 00:36:13,666
Woo Su Bin.

461
00:36:13,766 --> 00:36:14,926
("Life Is Like a B-cut")

462
00:36:18,496 --> 00:36:19,736
Hey, Woo Su Bin.

463
00:36:21,936 --> 00:36:24,036
What is this? Is this how a person should live?

464
00:36:24,106 --> 00:36:25,906
This is a pigsty. Hey.

465
00:36:26,346 --> 00:36:29,076
Why do you always leave your socks mismatched?

466
00:36:29,146 --> 00:36:31,616
And what are you doing right now?

467
00:36:31,816 --> 00:36:34,386
The film festival crew is coming soon.

468
00:36:34,446 --> 00:36:35,986
I told you I'm not doing it.

469
00:36:36,056 --> 00:36:38,856
You just have to give a short greeting.

470
00:36:38,916 --> 00:36:41,225
- I don't want to. - You don't want to?

471
00:36:41,226 --> 00:36:43,726
I really don't want to!

472
00:36:44,256 --> 00:36:46,295
Fine, if you’re going to complain, go get married, instead.

473
00:36:46,296 --> 00:36:48,366
Or at least write a script. What are you doing?

474
00:36:48,426 --> 00:36:49,566
Fine.

475
00:36:50,096 --> 00:36:53,366
- That's hilarious. Fine. - No, I'm not kidding.

476
00:36:53,506 --> 00:36:56,636
How long are you going to live like a jobless bum?

477
00:36:56,706 --> 00:36:58,806
I only make money when you work. Look at this.

478
00:36:58,876 --> 00:37:01,876
You rejected all these scripts you were offered.

479
00:37:02,146 --> 00:37:04,576
You know there's Director Park Jin Hyung...

480
00:37:04,646 --> 00:37:07,845
and Director Kim Sol. Tell them to work hard.

481
00:37:07,846 --> 00:37:11,316
Those two are already working hard to find a script.

482
00:37:11,656 --> 00:37:14,456
But you're the one who already has a script.

483
00:37:15,056 --> 00:37:18,726
- What script do I have? - "Dream". What you wrote in the US.

484
00:37:19,226 --> 00:37:21,366
- I see. - You remember that?

485
00:37:21,996 --> 00:37:23,596
I really loved that story.

486
00:37:23,666 --> 00:37:24,666
Let's make that one.

487
00:37:24,736 --> 00:37:26,536
- I don't have it. - You don't?

488
00:37:27,136 --> 00:37:29,176
- I gave it to Yi Jae. - You gave it to her?

489
00:37:29,476 --> 00:37:30,806
Did you scan it?

490
00:37:39,316 --> 00:37:40,616
Director Woo, we're breaking up.

491
00:37:40,686 --> 00:37:41,886
I think it's time we go our separate ways.

492
00:37:41,946 --> 00:37:45,116
I'm so sick of this. I can't do it anymore. Really.

493
00:37:46,256 --> 00:37:48,586
Either way, I go through a breakup every day.

494
00:37:52,526 --> 00:37:55,736
Hey, if Yi Jae found out you were living like this,

495
00:37:55,796 --> 00:37:57,166
she'd be so thrilled.

496
00:37:58,596 --> 00:38:00,166
At this year's Geumseong Film Festival,

497
00:38:00,336 --> 00:38:02,636
the hosts are Sim Yu Geon and Oh Ha Na.

498
00:38:02,706 --> 00:38:05,776
Well, they both won the Best New Actor Award last year,

499
00:38:06,376 --> 00:38:07,376
which is why Gyeongseong Love Song...

500
00:38:07,446 --> 00:38:09,316
is getting a special screening.

501
00:38:10,476 --> 00:38:11,476
Su Bin.

502
00:38:11,676 --> 00:38:14,616
I know what Gyeongseong Love Song means to you.

503
00:38:15,486 --> 00:38:16,586
Let's use this chance...

504
00:38:17,486 --> 00:38:19,456
to say a proper goodbye...

505
00:38:20,556 --> 00:38:21,886
and move on.

506
00:38:25,826 --> 00:38:26,826
In Wook.

507
00:38:28,726 --> 00:38:31,266
You can't stand me too?

508
00:38:32,566 --> 00:38:33,566
Am I pathetic?

509
00:38:37,436 --> 00:38:38,436
Fine.

510
00:38:39,976 --> 00:38:41,376
I think I'm pathetic too.

511
00:38:42,676 --> 00:38:45,746
Yi Jae can shine even without me.

512
00:38:47,246 --> 00:38:48,716
But I don't think I can.

513
00:38:52,556 --> 00:38:53,556
I'll do it.

514
00:38:58,956 --> 00:39:02,866
- Director. It's been a while. - It has been a while.

515
00:39:02,936 --> 00:39:04,465
- Have you been well? - Please, come in.

516
00:39:04,466 --> 00:39:05,966
We're here.

517
00:39:06,036 --> 00:39:08,006
- Hello. - You made it.

518
00:39:08,106 --> 00:39:09,436
Oh my gosh.

519
00:39:12,076 --> 00:39:13,306
Director Woo.

520
00:39:13,746 --> 00:39:16,676
- Well, look who it is. - Yes.

521
00:39:16,846 --> 00:39:19,516
You've met, right? He's in charge of filming today.

522
00:39:20,586 --> 00:39:22,656
Director, you don't remember me?

523
00:39:22,716 --> 00:39:25,456
Doesn't this look like the face of someone who remembers you?

524
00:39:27,386 --> 00:39:29,955
Goodness, you've gotten even pricklier.

525
00:39:29,956 --> 00:39:31,356
This is heavy.

526
00:39:32,256 --> 00:39:35,266
I left the network and started my own little production company.

527
00:39:36,866 --> 00:39:39,836
Let's have a good shoot today.

528
00:39:41,306 --> 00:39:45,206
Let's see. Where should we film?

529
00:39:45,376 --> 00:39:48,006
Gosh, the view here is killer.

530
00:39:48,076 --> 00:39:50,376
It'll be too cold if we shoot on the balcony.

531
00:39:50,516 --> 00:39:53,116
Here. This spot is good. This looks classy.

532
00:39:53,246 --> 00:39:55,516
- Let's do it here. - Okay.

533
00:39:55,686 --> 00:39:57,355
Would you like some coffee?

534
00:39:57,356 --> 00:39:59,325
Yes. I'm a die-hard iced Americano fan.

535
00:39:59,326 --> 00:40:00,586
Decaf, please.

536
00:40:07,596 --> 00:40:08,796
Is there no script?

537
00:40:08,866 --> 00:40:11,866
No. You said it will play before the screening, right?

538
00:40:11,966 --> 00:40:13,166
How many seconds should it be?

539
00:40:13,236 --> 00:40:16,036
About one minute is fine.

540
00:40:16,236 --> 00:40:17,336
But...

541
00:40:18,476 --> 00:40:21,006
Where is Joo Yi Jae? I don't see her.

542
00:40:21,976 --> 00:40:23,846
Oh, dear.

543
00:40:24,546 --> 00:40:25,816
You two split up?

544
00:40:26,346 --> 00:40:28,786
Well, she is a bit tough to work with.

545
00:40:28,846 --> 00:40:30,216
Yi Jae is...

546
00:40:30,616 --> 00:40:33,386
- shooting in Canada. - Canada?

547
00:40:34,756 --> 00:40:37,926
She really owes me a meal for that. Right?

548
00:40:38,796 --> 00:40:40,866
- Excuse me? - Just a moment.

549
00:40:41,926 --> 00:40:43,766
But Director,

550
00:40:43,836 --> 00:40:46,506
your style has gotten really laid-back since I last saw you.

551
00:40:47,106 --> 00:40:49,136
Now you finally look like a real director.

552
00:40:49,376 --> 00:40:51,675
- Are you shooting these days too? - Producer Gyeong.

553
00:40:51,676 --> 00:40:54,776
- Yes? - Aren't you going to start filming?

554
00:40:55,746 --> 00:40:57,046
Shouldn't we be filming now?

555
00:40:57,376 --> 00:40:59,945
I was just about to. Of course.

556
00:40:59,946 --> 00:41:01,216
Let's take off the hood.

557
00:41:01,746 --> 00:41:03,016
I'll do it.

558
00:41:03,056 --> 00:41:04,916
Okay. Please just take off the hood.

559
00:41:13,866 --> 00:41:18,366
- Why are you so late? - Oh, my gosh, look who it is.

560
00:41:18,866 --> 00:41:20,365
I missed you so much.

561
00:41:20,366 --> 00:41:22,776
How did you get so pretty? I almost didn't recognise you.

562
00:41:53,006 --> 00:41:54,536
Hi.

563
00:42:06,116 --> 00:42:07,116
Hey.

564
00:42:08,016 --> 00:42:09,586
I thought you were in Canada.

565
00:42:09,886 --> 00:42:12,726
- You're looking good. - What are you doing here?

566
00:42:12,786 --> 00:42:14,656
I'm just here today to...

567
00:42:23,636 --> 00:42:25,696
Hey, wait.

568
00:42:26,736 --> 00:42:28,236
I can't breathe.

569
00:42:31,276 --> 00:42:34,046
Oh, right. I was in the middle of making coffee.

570
00:42:34,106 --> 00:42:35,746
- That's right. Coffee. - I'll do it.

571
00:42:35,806 --> 00:42:36,875
Where is the camera?

572
00:42:36,876 --> 00:42:38,975
- I want to film this scene. - Wait.

573
00:42:38,976 --> 00:42:42,286
Coffee is ready. I made it nice and cold.

574
00:42:42,346 --> 00:42:44,416
- I wanted decaf. - Baby. Where are you?

575
00:42:44,986 --> 00:42:48,886
A bistro? Day drinking? Soju again?

576
00:42:53,726 --> 00:42:54,866
It's really you.

577
00:42:56,666 --> 00:42:57,996
It's really Joo Yi Jae.

578
00:42:58,796 --> 00:43:00,006
How have you been?

579
00:43:09,146 --> 00:43:10,876
What is all this?

580
00:43:10,946 --> 00:43:12,676
You haven't even opened the curtains in the middle of the day.

581
00:43:13,246 --> 00:43:16,016
What a mess.

582
00:43:16,056 --> 00:43:17,616
And you used to be such a neat freak.

583
00:43:19,216 --> 00:43:20,326
When did you get back?

584
00:43:20,986 --> 00:43:21,986
Early this morning.

585
00:43:24,256 --> 00:43:25,256
Why?

586
00:43:25,926 --> 00:43:27,326
Why do you think I'm here?

587
00:43:29,296 --> 00:43:31,496
The Geumseong Film Festival opens in two weeks.

588
00:43:31,896 --> 00:43:34,406
I'm nominated for the Best New Director Award there.

589
00:43:35,666 --> 00:43:36,676
I see.

590
00:43:38,606 --> 00:43:40,376
What? Aren't you going to congratulate me?

591
00:43:41,306 --> 00:43:44,046
Are you going back after the film festival?

592
00:43:44,476 --> 00:43:47,116
Well, I guess that depends on you.

593
00:43:50,686 --> 00:43:53,386
What do you want me to do?

594
00:43:54,586 --> 00:43:55,856
Do you have a girlfriend?

595
00:43:58,626 --> 00:43:59,866
I guess not, right?

596
00:44:01,726 --> 00:44:03,966
- Want to make a movie with me? - What?

597
00:44:09,906 --> 00:44:11,436
("Dream", written by Woo Su Bin)

598
00:44:12,076 --> 00:44:13,646
I didn't find out until I went to Canada.

599
00:44:13,946 --> 00:44:15,506
That you wrote my letter of recommendation.

600
00:44:16,976 --> 00:44:20,746
I think now I've grown enough to stand proudly by your side.

601
00:44:21,786 --> 00:44:23,786
Let's make a movie together, Woo Su Bin.

602
00:44:26,186 --> 00:44:27,456
Can I kiss you?

603
00:44:27,786 --> 00:44:28,786
Are you going to?

604
00:44:28,886 --> 00:44:29,896
Yes.

605
00:44:30,696 --> 00:44:33,596
No, are you going to make the movie with me?

606
00:44:39,636 --> 00:44:40,636
Yes.

607
00:44:47,906 --> 00:44:49,246
Directors.

608
00:44:50,346 --> 00:44:52,646
What's taking you so long?

609
00:44:53,216 --> 00:44:55,616
Please, I want to go home.

610
00:44:58,656 --> 00:45:01,126
- They're not coming out. - Well...

611
00:45:01,356 --> 00:45:02,556
Directors.

612
00:45:03,496 --> 00:45:05,126
What's taking you so long?

613
00:45:11,836 --> 00:45:15,006
The Best New Director Award at the 16th Geumseong Film Festival.

614
00:45:15,436 --> 00:45:16,536
And the winner is...

615
00:45:19,606 --> 00:45:21,576
Director Joo Yi Jae for "A Dreamlike Love".

616
00:45:21,646 --> 00:45:22,846
Congratulations.

617
00:45:23,346 --> 00:45:24,546
In her film "A Dreamlike Love", which she completed...

618
00:45:24,616 --> 00:45:27,016
through the International Cinema Residency Program,

619
00:45:27,046 --> 00:45:29,316
Director Joo Yi Jae portrayed a fantastical world...

620
00:45:29,386 --> 00:45:31,856
between dreams and reality convincingly...

621
00:45:31,916 --> 00:45:34,326
with her unique directorial style,

622
00:45:34,386 --> 00:45:35,856
for which she has been highly praised.

623
00:45:42,726 --> 00:45:44,196
Congratulations, Yi Jae.

624
00:45:48,066 --> 00:45:49,636
I've won an award!

625
00:45:49,706 --> 00:45:52,436
(Best New Director Award)

626
00:45:54,446 --> 00:45:55,646
Thank you.

627
00:45:58,416 --> 00:45:59,946
"A Dreamlike Love"...

628
00:46:00,316 --> 00:46:02,446
was a bold endeavour for me.

629
00:46:02,586 --> 00:46:04,386
My first time directing solo,

630
00:46:04,656 --> 00:46:06,726
writing a screenplay in an unfamiliar place,

631
00:46:06,786 --> 00:46:09,826
and communicating with an international staff.

632
00:46:10,856 --> 00:46:12,996
Honestly, it was really hard.

633
00:46:14,296 --> 00:46:16,696
But there was only one reason I was able to endure it.

634
00:46:18,266 --> 00:46:19,836
I wanted to become a better person...

635
00:46:20,506 --> 00:46:23,806
so I could stand next to the one I love.

636
00:46:25,976 --> 00:46:28,176
I loved my dream passionately.

637
00:46:28,946 --> 00:46:29,976
All right.

638
00:46:30,576 --> 00:46:32,376
Let's do something great together.

639
00:46:32,846 --> 00:46:33,846
Come here.

640
00:46:33,916 --> 00:46:35,816
Stop!

641
00:46:35,986 --> 00:46:38,286
I hated it as much as I loved it.

642
00:46:39,556 --> 00:46:40,726
You jerk.

643
00:46:43,756 --> 00:46:45,496
I tried to forget it,

644
00:46:45,726 --> 00:46:47,126
but in the end, I came back.

645
00:46:47,596 --> 00:46:49,096
Excuse me.

646
00:46:56,736 --> 00:46:59,306
Right now, I feel as if...

647
00:47:00,006 --> 00:47:01,706
I've been through a war-like love...

648
00:47:01,776 --> 00:47:03,776
and dramatically reconciled.

649
00:47:05,846 --> 00:47:07,146
From now on,

650
00:47:07,686 --> 00:47:10,756
there may be times we want to kill each other,

651
00:47:11,286 --> 00:47:12,756
but I'm not worried...

652
00:47:13,856 --> 00:47:14,856
because...

653
00:47:15,786 --> 00:47:17,726
I've become a bigger person.

654
00:47:20,066 --> 00:47:24,766
This love, which is like a war, I'll do my best to see it through.

655
00:47:25,696 --> 00:47:26,766
Thank you!

656
00:48:32,736 --> 00:48:35,066
Ready, action!

657
00:48:40,506 --> 00:48:44,376
Hey, stop filming and try this.

658
00:48:47,616 --> 00:48:50,186
- Good. It's perfect. - Is it salty enough?

659
00:48:50,216 --> 00:48:51,216
Yes.

660
00:48:51,956 --> 00:48:53,756
There we go.

661
00:48:56,696 --> 00:48:58,556
- Mom. - What is it?

662
00:48:58,756 --> 00:49:01,526
Is there anything you want to do?

663
00:49:02,196 --> 00:49:03,336
Why the sudden question?

664
00:49:03,636 --> 00:49:06,266
Su Bin's mother and the lady from the guesthouse...

665
00:49:06,336 --> 00:49:07,936
travel together all the time.

666
00:49:08,366 --> 00:49:10,836
Mom, do you want to go on a trip with me for a week?

667
00:49:11,076 --> 00:49:12,076
No, that's okay.

668
00:49:12,606 --> 00:49:14,946
If I close up the restaurant, I'll lose customers.

669
00:49:15,346 --> 00:49:17,346
Then let's just close the restaurant.

670
00:49:18,046 --> 00:49:19,546
Yeong Jae is earning money now.

671
00:49:20,786 --> 00:49:21,816
Yi Jae.

672
00:49:24,686 --> 00:49:27,026
I was always so caught up in making a living...

673
00:49:27,386 --> 00:49:29,456
that I was never happy running this place.

674
00:49:30,796 --> 00:49:33,466
Opening the restaurant every morning felt like a huge burden.

675
00:49:34,966 --> 00:49:36,836
But lately, it feels lighter.

676
00:49:39,266 --> 00:49:42,336
Both you and Yeong Jae have found your way in life,

677
00:49:42,736 --> 00:49:44,506
so I can finally rest easy.

678
00:49:46,676 --> 00:49:49,346
For now, I'm just going to enjoy running the restaurant.

679
00:49:52,616 --> 00:49:55,546
When I get sick of it, I'll quit. Okay?

680
00:49:59,356 --> 00:50:02,326
Once you quit, you have to go on that trip with me.

681
00:50:02,586 --> 00:50:03,596
Okay.

682
00:50:04,356 --> 00:50:05,356
Promise me.

683
00:50:06,696 --> 00:50:09,296
- Hey, what's with your hand? - What?

684
00:50:14,166 --> 00:50:15,966
Well, I'm heading out.

685
00:50:16,536 --> 00:50:17,536
Where are you going?

686
00:50:18,106 --> 00:50:19,106
To see Su Bin.

687
00:50:19,536 --> 00:50:21,876
- Hey, Yi Jae. - Yes?

688
00:50:21,976 --> 00:50:23,246
I asked for an autograph,

689
00:50:23,316 --> 00:50:24,816
not for you to just run your mouth and leave.

690
00:50:25,016 --> 00:50:26,376
Oh, that's right.

691
00:50:28,946 --> 00:50:32,886
- Oh, my. - Here it is. Right here.

692
00:50:34,926 --> 00:50:35,926
Wait.

693
00:50:37,156 --> 00:50:40,496
Do all these people know me?

694
00:50:40,566 --> 00:50:42,966
Of course. Director Joo Yi Jae.

695
00:50:44,866 --> 00:50:47,336
I doubt they've even seen my movie.

696
00:50:47,606 --> 00:50:49,166
They haven't.

697
00:50:50,236 --> 00:50:51,236
What?

698
00:50:51,436 --> 00:50:54,506
That's why I told them they're only for people who've seen your movie.

699
00:50:55,446 --> 00:50:56,446
I knew it.

700
00:50:58,346 --> 00:51:00,116
- Here you go. - The autograph.

701
00:51:00,716 --> 00:51:03,316
"Gyeongseong Love Song".

702
00:51:03,386 --> 00:51:04,456
"Director".

703
00:51:05,016 --> 00:51:06,786
"Joo Yi Jae".

704
00:51:07,026 --> 00:51:08,056
What do you think?

705
00:51:08,626 --> 00:51:10,896
- It's cool. - You think so?

706
00:51:12,996 --> 00:51:15,166
Are the lady from the guesthouse and your mom coming today?

707
00:51:15,466 --> 00:51:17,936
- They should be here by now. - I see.

708
00:51:24,206 --> 00:51:27,506
- Kids, we're here. - Hello!

709
00:51:27,676 --> 00:51:31,316
- Son, Yi Jae, get in. - Get in.

710
00:51:37,956 --> 00:51:40,056
- Let's go. - Let's go.

711
00:51:40,386 --> 00:51:42,385
- I have something to show you. - Don't even ask.

712
00:51:42,386 --> 00:51:43,656
It was such a hassle.

713
00:51:43,726 --> 00:51:45,996
(Today, I went to see the ocean with Hwa Yeon.)

714
00:51:46,226 --> 00:51:47,726
You went all the way to Gangneung?

715
00:51:49,266 --> 00:51:51,666
I thought one beach is the same as any other,

716
00:51:51,936 --> 00:51:54,206
but the sea there was completely different.

717
00:51:55,036 --> 00:51:57,276
The waves here are calm, just like me.

718
00:51:57,336 --> 00:51:59,276
As if they've lived a full life.

719
00:51:59,406 --> 00:52:01,906
But the ones in Gangneung...

720
00:52:02,206 --> 00:52:04,076
were so blue and fierce, just like the two of you.

721
00:52:05,176 --> 00:52:08,486
Oh, but in my eyes, you were just like the waves in Gangneung.

722
00:52:08,886 --> 00:52:09,886
What?

723
00:52:10,486 --> 00:52:12,286
Right before she left,

724
00:52:12,356 --> 00:52:15,386
she was grumbling about being too old to go anywhere.

725
00:52:15,626 --> 00:52:16,826
But once she got there,

726
00:52:18,356 --> 00:52:20,866
she had more energy than I did.

727
00:52:21,566 --> 00:52:23,666
I can't travel with Hwa Yeon.

728
00:52:24,036 --> 00:52:26,566
She wants to rest after walking for just 30 minutes...

729
00:52:26,636 --> 00:52:27,866
and says we should get coffee.

730
00:52:28,736 --> 00:52:30,576
You're supposed to be sightseeing when you travel.

731
00:52:30,706 --> 00:52:32,176
If you're just going to drink coffee...

732
00:52:32,436 --> 00:52:34,446
and sit around, why go in the first place?

733
00:52:34,676 --> 00:52:35,676
Isn't that right?

734
00:52:36,146 --> 00:52:38,616
That's right. You're right about that.

735
00:52:38,816 --> 00:52:40,115
- Oh, honestly. - Ma'am.

736
00:52:40,116 --> 00:52:42,116
Where do you want to go for your next trip?

737
00:52:43,556 --> 00:52:46,286
I still want to go to the US.

738
00:52:47,126 --> 00:52:49,286
I want to fly on a plane at least once before I die.

739
00:52:50,726 --> 00:52:51,896
Go with me.

740
00:52:52,456 --> 00:52:55,126
No, I'm not going with you.

741
00:52:55,866 --> 00:52:59,296
- You'll be sad. - Sad about what?

742
00:52:59,696 --> 00:53:01,666
- Let's go together. - Then, go with me.

743
00:53:02,936 --> 00:53:05,036
- Oh, my. - Yi Jae, join us.

744
00:53:05,306 --> 00:53:08,446
So the main character finally manages to escape,

745
00:53:08,646 --> 00:53:09,706
but here's the twist.

746
00:53:09,946 --> 00:53:11,416
The ending credits start rolling right before...

747
00:53:11,476 --> 00:53:13,986
the main character's eyes. Along with the game company's logo.

748
00:53:14,046 --> 00:53:15,316
Chills!

749
00:53:15,716 --> 00:53:18,386
It was all inside a game. What do you think?

750
00:53:18,416 --> 00:53:19,916
Do you get the feeling it's going to work out?

751
00:53:21,426 --> 00:53:24,596
I'm telling you, this would be a blockbuster movie.

752
00:53:24,626 --> 00:53:26,126
This braised radish is delicious today, isn't it?

753
00:53:26,296 --> 00:53:28,495
- Try this too. - Hey, just listen.

754
00:53:28,496 --> 00:53:29,766
This is my dream.

755
00:53:29,826 --> 00:53:32,666
- Making a movie based on my novel. - Kim Jin Su.

756
00:53:35,036 --> 00:53:36,236
Yi Jae.

757
00:53:39,506 --> 00:53:40,976
- Hey, you troublemaker. - Sung Chan.

758
00:53:41,046 --> 00:53:42,706
- Didn't I tell you to pick him up? - Yi Jae.

759
00:53:43,176 --> 00:53:45,646
- Oh, that's right. - "Oh, that's right"?

760
00:53:45,746 --> 00:53:47,286
And you're here talking about your dream.

761
00:53:47,716 --> 00:53:50,756
My dream is for you to become a decent person, got it?

762
00:53:50,816 --> 00:53:51,855
Where do you think you're going?

763
00:53:51,856 --> 00:53:53,486
Today, I'm going to make you into a real person.

764
00:53:53,556 --> 00:53:54,556
Hey, let go of me.

765
00:53:54,626 --> 00:53:57,056
One way or another, I'll do it. Come here. Look at this, will you?

766
00:53:57,126 --> 00:54:00,026
- What's that? - This? It's a camera.

767
00:54:00,796 --> 00:54:02,996
- Want to see? - You punk!

768
00:54:03,066 --> 00:54:05,536
That scene looks a little too violent for a kid.

769
00:54:06,236 --> 00:54:09,266
It's okay. I'm in elementary school now.

770
00:54:10,406 --> 00:54:13,006
Sung Chan. What do you want to be when you grow up?

771
00:54:13,336 --> 00:54:16,346
My mom told me not to be anything like my dad.

772
00:54:18,616 --> 00:54:21,346
- The spicy fish stew is delicious. - We should come here again.

773
00:54:21,416 --> 00:54:23,716
- This is my favourite restaurant. - I'm so full.

774
00:54:23,986 --> 00:54:24,986
(Simsim Seafood)

775
00:54:25,456 --> 00:54:27,886
Joo Yeong Jae.

776
00:54:29,986 --> 00:54:32,326
You're here. Please, have a seat.

777
00:54:33,226 --> 00:54:34,926
He's impressive. It must be tough doing this alone.

778
00:54:35,326 --> 00:54:36,736
He's my brother. Why are you so impressed?

779
00:54:37,866 --> 00:54:39,396
Is my brother-in-law a stranger to me?

780
00:54:39,896 --> 00:54:40,936
What?

781
00:54:41,866 --> 00:54:42,936
I should give him a hand.

782
00:54:43,536 --> 00:54:44,976
Brother-in-law, let me give you a hand.

783
00:54:45,036 --> 00:54:46,336
No, please, just sit down.

784
00:54:46,406 --> 00:54:47,675
- Let me help. - No, it's all right.

785
00:54:47,676 --> 00:54:49,706
Please sit down. Please, just sit.

786
00:54:50,346 --> 00:54:51,346
I can just help with this, right?

787
00:54:51,646 --> 00:54:55,446
Unbelievable. "Brother-in-law"? Seriously.

788
00:55:00,016 --> 00:55:01,056
My dear brother-in-law.

789
00:55:02,256 --> 00:55:04,626
- I love you. - Okay.

790
00:55:08,266 --> 00:55:10,166
But there's one thing I'm curious about.

791
00:55:10,666 --> 00:55:11,696
Yes?

792
00:55:12,036 --> 00:55:13,266
Didn't you miss me?

793
00:55:13,936 --> 00:55:15,236
Do you even have to ask?

794
00:55:15,636 --> 00:55:17,136
Then why didn't I hear from you at all?

795
00:55:17,206 --> 00:55:18,806
That's cold.

796
00:55:19,136 --> 00:55:21,146
- But I did contact you. - What?

797
00:55:21,946 --> 00:55:23,515
- It's nothing. - So did you...

798
00:55:23,516 --> 00:55:26,116
skip meals, lose sleep, and get drunk and cry about it?

799
00:55:27,386 --> 00:55:31,316
What do you take me for? It wasn't quite like that.

800
00:55:34,526 --> 00:55:38,126
- Joo Yi... - This guy's making a scene again.

801
00:55:38,196 --> 00:55:39,196
Good grief.

802
00:55:39,856 --> 00:55:40,866
Don't disappear.

803
00:55:42,066 --> 00:55:43,066
No.

804
00:55:43,126 --> 00:55:44,866
It's telepathy.

805
00:55:45,896 --> 00:55:46,936
Joo Yi Jae.

806
00:55:47,906 --> 00:55:50,106
Get over here right now.

807
00:55:51,206 --> 00:55:52,336
Come here now.

808
00:55:53,176 --> 00:55:56,976
- Mom, that man is weird. - It's not polite to stare.

809
00:55:57,476 --> 00:55:59,045
Get over here right now!

810
00:55:59,046 --> 00:56:00,216
You slept here again?

811
00:56:00,886 --> 00:56:02,346
I used to make hangover soup for my daughter.

812
00:56:02,416 --> 00:56:03,416
Goodness gracious.

813
00:56:03,486 --> 00:56:05,716
And now, do I have to make hangover soup for you too?

814
00:56:06,416 --> 00:56:09,326
Good morning. Why did she go there?

815
00:56:11,396 --> 00:56:15,326
(Jaejae Noodles)

816
00:56:21,906 --> 00:56:23,036
So...

817
00:56:23,136 --> 00:56:24,676
(Jaejae Noodles)

818
00:56:24,776 --> 00:56:26,036
I was very patiently waiting for you.

819
00:56:26,876 --> 00:56:28,146
So you did wait for me, then.

820
00:56:30,146 --> 00:56:31,546
Of course.

821
00:56:32,976 --> 00:56:34,046
I knew you'd come back.

822
00:56:34,746 --> 00:56:36,416
What if I had decided to stay in Canada?

823
00:56:36,516 --> 00:56:38,416
I would've reported you for being there illegally.

824
00:56:38,756 --> 00:56:40,256
And what if I stayed legally?

825
00:56:40,856 --> 00:56:42,156
Then I would've just gone to you.

826
00:56:43,286 --> 00:56:44,826
What if I wasn't happy to see you?

827
00:56:45,996 --> 00:56:48,226
Why wouldn't you be happy to see me?

828
00:56:48,666 --> 00:56:50,996
Well, what if I had a new boyfriend?

829
00:56:51,496 --> 00:56:54,906
A handsome boyfriend, or a sexy boyfriend?

830
00:56:56,906 --> 00:56:57,906
More than me?

831
00:57:02,006 --> 00:57:04,416
Goodbye then. Mr. Sexy and Handsome, Woo Su Bin.

832
00:57:08,946 --> 00:57:09,946
Yi Jae.

833
00:57:15,326 --> 00:57:16,326
Will you...

834
00:57:17,656 --> 00:57:18,726
stay with me tonight?

835
00:57:45,586 --> 00:57:46,586
Come on, let's go.

836
00:58:26,696 --> 00:58:29,266
- That tickles. - Bear with it.

837
00:58:35,206 --> 00:58:36,206
What?

838
00:58:37,276 --> 00:58:38,576
I thought I lost this.

839
00:58:39,906 --> 00:58:41,445
Go ahead and tie your hair up with this...

840
00:58:41,446 --> 00:58:42,506
and continue what you were doing.

841
00:58:43,246 --> 00:58:45,916
Wait a minute. Were you at the airport that day?

842
00:58:48,646 --> 00:58:49,646
Yes.

843
00:58:51,686 --> 00:58:52,856
And...

844
00:58:54,126 --> 00:58:55,126
one more thing.

845
00:58:57,526 --> 00:58:58,526
This.

846
00:59:09,066 --> 00:59:10,066
What is this?

847
00:59:15,776 --> 00:59:16,776
My dream.

848
00:59:20,886 --> 00:59:21,886
Cut.

849
00:59:22,716 --> 00:59:23,716
Cut?

850
00:59:44,106 --> 00:59:45,106
Okay.

851
00:59:45,436 --> 00:59:46,436
Okay.

852
00:59:56,446 --> 01:00:02,326
("Dream", Written by Woo Su Bin and Joo Yi Jae)

853
01:00:12,766 --> 01:00:15,736
(We thank our viewers who have loved and supported Dream To You.)

854
01:00:46,666 --> 01:00:48,666
(Dream To You)